A partly visible scalable (SVG / display-list) image is drawn where it
belongs. Applies on top of 0057-scalable-image-device-size.

When only part of the image is visible (a tile of a zoomed page, an image
running off the page), the draw device asks fz_get_pixmap_from_image() for
just that subarea. For other images the ctm is then mapped to the subarea
(update_ctm_for_subarea); the scalable branch returned the subarea's pixmap
with the whole image's ctm, so it was stretched over the whole image.
(Idea from Vira Reader's mupdf-scalable-image-subarea.patch.)

diff --git a/source/fitz/image.c b/source/fitz/image.c
index 6a16d5175..2803b7619 100644
--- a/source/fitz/image.c
+++ b/source/fitz/image.c
@@ -1067,7 +1067,13 @@ fz_get_pixmap_from_image(fz_context *ctx, fz_image *image, const fz_irect *subar
 		}
 		if (dw) *dw = w;
 		if (dh) *dh = h;
-		return image->get_pixmap(ctx, image, subarea ? &subarea_copy : NULL, w, h, &l2factor_remaining);
+		tile = image->get_pixmap(ctx, image, subarea ? &subarea_copy : NULL, w, h, &l2factor_remaining);
+		/* SumatraPDF: the pixmap is only the subarea; map the image's unit
+		 * square to it, as for other images, or it is stretched over the
+		 * whole image (idea from Vira Reader). */
+		if (subarea)
+			update_ctm_for_subarea(ctm, &subarea_copy, image->w, image->h);
+		return tile;
 	}
 
 	/* Clamp requested image size, since we never want to magnify images here. */
